<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλυψ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠβος</span>, ὁ, in pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Chalybes</i> in Pontus, who
			were famous for the preparation of steel, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ σιδηροτέκτονες Χάλυβες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					715
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.5.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				9.1092.48
			</span></i> (on another nation of the same name v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				12.3.20
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Appellat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλυψ,</span>
			<i>hardened iron, steel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				133
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1260
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Antip.Sid.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				662.52
			</span></i>; of a <i>penknife,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.65
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Sil.
			</span></i>); of an <i>axe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				APl.
				4.127
			</span></i>: as Adj., <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				36.182
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάλυβος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, Χάλυβος Σκυθῶν ἄποικος,</span> i. e.
				<i>steel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				728
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χαλύβῳ πελέκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					472.6
				</span></i>
			 (anap.): pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάλυβες</span>
			, E.ap.Sch.Il.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1087 i 28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἐν Χαλύβοις σίδαρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					980
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
